    "summary": "High‑energy UCLA ’82 show with blazing Shakedown Street and soaring Stella Blue",
    "review": "The February 21, 1982 Pauley Pavilion concert is a quintessential early‑'80s Dead experience – the band rides a high‑octane groove from the opening “Shakedown Street” straight through a tight second set. Jerry is on fire, delivering a scorching solo on “Tiger” and crisp leads throughout; Phil drops bass bombs that lift the NFA → Stella Blue transition into something special, while Brent’s keyboards add texture without getting lost in the mix. The rhythm section – Bill and Mickey – lock in tight, especially during the memorable drums‑and‑space segment that feeds directly into a powerful “Not Fade Away” and a beautifully sung “Stella Blue.” Even though one source omits the “China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider” pair, the overall flow stays strong, making this show a must‑listen for anyone chasing that early‑'80s fire.",
